  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\u27e8\\sqrt{4-t},\\,{t}^{2}-1,\\,(t-2)^{3}\u27e9.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\sqrt{4-t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,4].$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component ${t}^{2}-1$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $(t-2)^{3}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/assets/af217bfbda3db04572cbfbb0b1aa8c18a6bb94c127c3d034dbfe3d96d6abbf80.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,4].$",
